WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.267
-Welcome to the show.
-God, that was so cool.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:05.434
-I'm so happy you're here.
-Oh, my God, that was epic.

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.534
-Come on! Yes, that was epic.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.534 --> 00:00:09.868
Thank you for being on the show.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.667
-Your show "Never Have I Ever,"
by the way,

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:14.534
is a giant, giant hit
on Netflix.

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.234
It was co-created by
Mindy Kaling.

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:18.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes.

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:21.400
-I just want to say, it hit
number 1 in over 50 countries,

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.801
so not too shabby right there.

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:24.801
Congratulations on that.
-Thank you.

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:26.667
-It's --
You're very, very funny.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:29.567
And growing up,
were you always funny?

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:31.901
-I mean,
I'm the youngest sibling,

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:33.467
so I had, like,
the usual antics.

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:36.467
Yeah, younger-sibling energy.
Let's go. Right?

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:38.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.567
Obviously stole a lot of
my mom's clothes.

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:43.934
You know, try to show up,
be center of attention.

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:45.033
Definitely made all of

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:47.234
my brother's
birthday parties about me.

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:49.434
Everyone's always looking at
my brother, you know?

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:51.801
"Happy birthday.
Good job, Vishwaa."

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:53.601
And I'm looking directly
into the camera,

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:56.167
making faces like...

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:57.934
Why did I do that? I don't know.

00:00:57.934 --> 00:00:59.834
-Yeah. But now you're
a big star of a comedy.

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.334
-Yeah, apparently.

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.868
-Yeah. And this was like the
first big gig for you, right?

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:05.501
-First job.
-First job?

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:07.334
-Yeah. I really wanted
a part-time job

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:09.767
when I was in high school,
but I did not have the time.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:13.634
Depression naps took over,
so -- Yeah.

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:16.167
-Depression naps.
-Yes, exactly.

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:17.501
So, this is my first job.

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:18.868
-And then, yeah, this is --

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:22.601
Look at the young Maitreyi
right there.

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:23.901
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:26.133
-Oh, you do not need to
say "Aww" to that.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:27.601
-No, no.
-This dork?

00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:28.968
-That might be the cutest photo

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.434
we've ever shown on
"The Tonight Show."

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:31.534
Come on!

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:34.434
-That's joy.
This girl has it together.

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:36.033
She has it together.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:37.167
-She really does
have it together.

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.534
But now here you are.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:41.367
You get in there, you go,
you're on -- Is Mindy --

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.234
Are you getting advice from
Mindy Kaling?

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:44.634
-Yes, yes.

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:47.400
My favorite thing, though,
is to try and convince people

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.234
that we're distantly related,
because then they feel awkward.

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:53.434
They're like, "Oh, yeah, because
you guys are both brown,

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:55.801
like, yeah, you guys have
got to be related."

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:57.868
And then they're like,
"Oh, yeah, that makes sense."

00:01:57.868 --> 00:02:00.968
And I'm like, "No, no.
I just totally made that up."

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:02.133
-Yeah, totally made that up.

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:03.534
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:07.200
But I love that your voice in
the show -- no spoilers --

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.067
but your voiceover is
the voice of John McEnroe.

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:11.400
-Yeah. Good old McEnroe.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.167
-And that is genius, by the way.

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:14.801
Did Mindy think of -- I don't
know whoever thought of that.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.367
-Well, John McEnroe
is really important to Mindy.

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.200
And I think it's, like,
a great match made in heaven.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.367
-He's important to everyone.

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:23.100
-Yeah, I think
he's important to everyone.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.968
He's important to me
now that I know who he is.

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:29.033
-You didn't at first?
-I didn't know.

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:30.701
I'm not a sports kind of gal.

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:33.067
-Oh, he's a legend.
-He's a legend. He is.

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:34.467
He is.
-A living legend.

00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:36.033
He's unbelievable. And funny.

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:40.067
-I know him as a narrating
legend, not necessarily tennis.

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:42.534
And, actually, funny story.

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:45.534
On set, when I met him,
I was like,

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:48.934
"Hey, do you, like, still sport?

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.734
Like, do you sports?"
-Do you sports?

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:52.601
-Like, "Do you sports?"

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:54.100
You know? I don't know.
-Do you sports?

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.868
-Maybe he's, like, taking a
break. I don't know.

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:57.434
I'm just trying to make
conversation with friends.

00:02:57.434 --> 00:02:58.901
-Yeah, of course, yes.

00:02:58.901 --> 00:03:00.834
And, so, John McEnroe
is like, "Yeah."

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.067
-And he's like, "Yeah.
Yeah, I do."

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:03.367
And I'm like,
"Oh, cool, cool, cool, cool.

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:06.400
I don't really sport,
so, like, guess I can't relate."

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.267
-"I don't sport."
-I don't do sports.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:09.467
-Yeah.

00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:10.667
-And then I asked him
if he wanted to go to

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:12.133
crafty and get cookies,
and he said, "Yeah."

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:13.868
-Yeah. He's the best.
-So it was great.

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:15.534
-This is the third season here,

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:18.267
and then you've been renewed for
a fourth and final season.

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:19.634
-Yes, fourth and final.
-Congratulations on that.

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:20.868
That's great.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:23.100
-Thank you.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.767
Here is Maitreyi Ramakrishnan in
"Never Have I Ever."

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:27.067
Take a look at this.

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:29.033
-So, you want to go to
dinner this weekend?

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.133
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:31.567
Like,
heat up your mom's leftovers

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:33.100
and play "Fortnite" in your
garage with Trent and Marcus?

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.234
Sure.

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:36.334
-Damn. Is that what
our dates are like?

00:03:36.334 --> 00:03:38.167
-Mm-hmm.
-That sucks.

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:42.567
No, like a real date,
like romantic.

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:44.834
Have you ever been to CPK?

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:48.234
-CPK? A.K.A.
California Pizza Kitchen?

00:03:48.234 --> 00:03:52.200
Only the preeminent fast-casual
pizza chain in the U.S.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.734
Now, that's a date.
I wish I could go.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.534
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:57.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.834 --> 00:04:01.434
-Eh? Eh?
-Maitreyi Ramakrishnan.

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:04.067
Season 3 of "Never Have I Ever"

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:06.501
begins streaming
this Friday on Netflix.

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:07.567
Please come back.

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:08.634
-Hell yeah.
-Love you, bud.

